sorted by it; choose &quot;Most recent&quot; in Sort, or tick &quot;Hot and warm only&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Why&quot; gives the three strongest reasons, for example &quot;Pickup tomorrow · Reached step 3 of the request form · Tapped to call&quot;. The badges are all the signals of the visit; the dots say how strong each is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each visitor also shows their name when known (signed in, or arrived from one of our emails), otherwise &quot;Visitor from Toronto, phone&quot;; the page and car they are on, and how many others look at that car now; the device, city, the site or campaign that sent them and &quot;from an ad&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Suggested: the best next step and the message to send. Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to chat with this message</b> to send it at once, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the message</b> to change it first, <b class="gd-ui">Offer a 10% discount code</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Assign to Sales</b> or, when their dates are taken, <b class="gd-ui">Suggest a similar free car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Pages</b> for every page and event of the visit with each signal&#39;s points, or <b class="gd-ui">Start a chat</b> to write your own message. They see it in a bubble and reply from it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Below: hot visitors today (and whether someone acted), the signals of the last 24 hours, and the most viewed cars of the week with prices shown and the car most compared with each. The page refreshes by itself every 15 seconds.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-name-a-visitor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Name a visitor</h2><p class="gd-p">When you learn who a visitor is (they called, or told you in the chat), give them a name. Only staff see it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On their line, press <b class="gd-ui">Name</b>. Type the name and, if you have them, their phone, email and a note. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the name</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The name shows on Visitors (Live now and History), the visit&#39;s pages and Live chat, and on every later visit from the same browser. The line says who named them, with the phone, email and note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A phone you add also saves them as a contact in Quo, and a call or text from that number shows the name in Texts and calls.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Kept consistent: if they later book or sign in, the name the booking has replaces yours (&quot;Booked&quot;). A chat from another browser with the same email or phone gets the same name, and a chat&#39;s email or phone fills in the ones you left empty.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit name</b> changes it; <b class="gd-ui">Remove the name</b> takes it off.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live map</h2><p class="gd-p">A map of the Greater Toronto Area from Hamilton at the bottom to Barrie at the top, Toronto in the middle, with a dot for every lead, made for a TV or monitor in the office. It reads like a real map: every city and town is outlined (the GTA&#39;s regions, Toronto, Peel, York, Durham, Halton and Hamilton, a little stronger), with the highways and the major roads, the cities&#39; names, a soft glow where people live and the Niagara Escarpment and the Oak Ridges Moraine as gentle ridges; the lake stays dark and quiet. A lead outside that area widens the map, keeping Toronto in the middle.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b>: the map is at the top. The four numbers: who is on the site now, requests today, cars on rent now and the money collected this month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each dot is one person, coloured by their stage: green on rent or booked, amber requests and forms (a request, a form sent or a form started), cyan on the site now or a game played, grey past renters. The stages under the map count each one; press one to hide or show it. Renters on rent, bookings and hot leads show as a small card with a photo of their car, framed in their stage colour (the make&#39;s initial when the car has no photo); a hot lead not yet booked has a rose ring. Cards that would cover each other move apart, with a fine line back to their place. Each card and dot carries the person&#39;s first name and last initial (&quot;Visitor in Mississauga&quot; when we do not know who it is). A visitor on the site breathes slowly, a new event sends one ripple, and crowded dots join in a count (press it to zoom in). Busy areas glow softly. The C marker is home base (the delivery origin in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>), with a thin line running to each car on rent or booked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Rest the pointer on a lead (a dot or a car card), or move to it with Tab, to preview its card; press it to keep the card open (on a phone or tablet, tap it). The card shows the full name, the stage, the score from 0 to 100 with every signal, the car they looked at last with its photo and daily price, the city, how long they were on the site or when they were last seen, and a link to open the booking, the rente