d under the map.</li><li>The score adds up the points of the signals: what they did (on rent, booking, request, form sent or started), a game played or its prize claimed, past rentals, a returning visit, pages, minutes on the site, cars viewed, on the site now, from an ad, and the strongest Live visitors reasons. 60 or more is hot, 30 or more warm.</li><li>No hardware acceleration: when the browser has WebGL turned off (in Chrome, Settings &gt; System &gt; Use graphics acceleration when available), the same map is drawn another way, a little slower, and a note in the corner says so. Turning hardware acceleration on makes it faster.</li><li>The fleet layer: once CarmaCars&#39; trackers report, each car shows on the map with its photo, the direction it is going and its status (on rent, available, in service). Tick <b class="gd-ui">Fleet</b> to show or hide it.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-past-visits-history" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Past visits (History)</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">History</b> under the map for the visits before now: who (a name when we know it), where they came from (the site, the search or the campaign, and &quot;ad&quot;), the first and last page, how many pages and cars, how long, the device and city, and what the visit led to (a request, a booking, an account, contact details). Filter by dates, what it led to, city and source or campaign; <b class="gd-ui">More filters</b> has the device, the landing page, the country, new or returning, and bots and staff. <b class="gd-ui">Totals and day by day</b> shows the dates&#39; visits, conversions, the chart and the top pages and sources. Press a visit&#39;s icon to see it on the map (when it is still there), or <b class="gd-ui">Open the visit</b> for every page and event. Visitor history and Live visitors are now this one page; their old links open it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-the-signals" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The signals</h2><p class="gd-p">Each signal adds points to the booking likelihood. They come from what the visitor does on the site, never from what they type.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Intent: dates searched again and again, saw the full price, reached the booking form (and which step), came back for the same car on another day, comparing two or three cars, read the cancellation policy, read about the deposit, insurance or requirements, tapped to call, text or WhatsApp us or copied our number, checked delivery, looked through many photos or stayed long on one car.</li><li>Urgency: pickup within 72 hours, weekend or holiday dates, on a phone late at night, came from a city or model page or a &quot;near me&quot; search.</li><li>Value: a weekly or monthly rental, a premium car, SUV or van, adding a driver, asked about young drivers, a business email.</li><li>Hesitation: watching the price (sorted by lowest price, lowered the price limit), left after seeing the price, unsure about the deposit, trouble with a form, the car not free for their dates.</li><li>Context: came from an ad, a past renter, an offer or payment waiting, a game code not used yet, a popular car. The signals of known customers (offer opened, pay page left, change proposal, request stopped, returning visitor, viewing spree) count too.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-hot-visitors-and-the-actions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hot visitors and the actions</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>When a visitor turns hot, everyone with Live visitors open sees an alert at the top of the page. Turn on desktop alerts in Live chat to get one on your computer too; none come in the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am). No email is sent.</li><li>A discount code is single use, 10% off the rental charge (at most $75), valid 3 days, one per visitor a week and 10 a day per person. Admins and Sales send them; the code goes in the chat with the message.</li><li>Assign to Sales gives the visitor to the Sales person on shift (or to you if you work Sales) and raises a task with the reasons and the contact when we know who they are.</li><li>Each action shows on the visitor (&quot;Invited by Lena, 2 min ago&quot;) so two people do not write to the same visitor.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-signal-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signal settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Signal settings</b> (above the Live now list).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Score and actions: from how many points a visitor is hot or warm, when a signal is strong or medium, the hot alert, and the discount code (percent, most off a booking, days valid, codes a day per person, whether customer service may send codes, and the message).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each signal: on or off, its points, its thresholds (for example 72 hours for &quot;Pickup soon&quot;, 3 searches for &quot;Searching dates again and again&quot;), the suggested action and the message. {car}, {days}, {pickup} and the other words in braces are filled in from the visit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the signals</b>. The next look at each visit uses them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-follow-up-tasks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Follow-up tasks</h2><p class="gd-p">Signals of known visitors become tasks with a suggested action, for example &quot;Call or message Maya Chen: opened offer CC-1042 twice, no answer for 6 hours&quot;.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>An offer opened and not answered: after 6 hours, to Sales when the booking is credited to someone in Sales, otherwise customer service.</li><li>The pay page left without paying: after 30 minutes, customer service. The change proposal opened twice: customer service.</li><li>A booking request started and stopped, or a viewing spree, by a known visitor: Sales.</li><li>A task closes by itself when the renter answers the offer, pays or answers the proposal. Each signal raises one task only.</li><li>The thresholds are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, group &quot;Live visitors and live chat&quot;, with how long &quot;on the site now&quot; lasts (5 minutes) and how often an open page says it is still there (45 seconds). Follow-ups done count in My sales.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-recovery-emails" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Recovery emails</h2><p class="gd-p">Known renters who stop before finishing get one polite reminder, and at most one more a day later.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>An offer opened and not answered: after 4 hours. The pay page left without paying: after an hour. A change proposal opened and not answered: after 4 hours.</li><li>A booking request started and not sent: after 2 hours, and only to renters who agreed to hear from us (marketing consent).</li><li>Sent only between 9:00 and 21:00 Toronto time, never to someone who unsubscribed, and never while a staff member is handling the renter (a task they took, a chat with a person, a message from staff).</li><li>They stop as soon as the renter answers, pays or sends the request; a reminder still waiting is not sent. The delays and hours are in Program settings, &quot;Booking recovery emails&quot;.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-interest-in-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interest in a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, a car, Overview: &quot;Interest on the site&quot; shows who is looking now, views today and in 7 days, the people who saw the price for their dates, conversion over 30 days (requests from the people who viewed it), the cars most often compared with it, and the last 14 days. The Vehicles list has &quot;Most viewed cars this week&quot;.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-a-renter-s-visits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A renter&#39;s visits</h2><p class="gd-p">On a renter&#39;s page (People &gt; Renters, the name) and on a booking&#39;s History tab, &quot;On the site&quot; lists when they viewed the offer, opened the change proposal, viewed or left the pay page, which cars they looked at, and their chats.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-live-chat" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live chat</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A visitor who asks for a person is a line on To do, marked Now: press <b class="gd-ui">Open the chat</b>. Or open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Live chat</b>. The menu counts the chats that need a reply: a chat waiting for a person, or one a person has where the visitor wrote last. Live chat shows the same number. Those chats come first, with their minutes against the first reply target (5 minutes).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a conversation. Beside it you see the visitor&#39;s page, pages, signals, and the renter with their bookings when known.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b>: the assistant stops and the visitor reads that you joined. Writing a reply also takes over. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or Enter).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hand back to the assistant</b> lets it answer again. <b class="gd-ui">Close</b> ends the chat; if the visitor gave an email they get a copy. <b class="gd-ui">Email the transcript</b> sends it any time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Alerts: each new visitor message that waits for staff sends one alert to the bell and, with phone alerts on, to your phone (topic Messages), on shift or not. A chat someone has goes to that person only. The alert clears when someone replies or the chat closes. &quot;Email me when a chat waits (while I am on shift)&quot; and desktop alerts in this browser are in Notify me.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The assistant only repeats prices from our pricing (a quote or the car&#39;s rates), never offers discounts or promises a car, never talks about insurance and never names a provider. Each reply it was not allowed to send says so in the conversation. When nobody is on shift, the chat asks for the visitor&#39;s name, email or phone and raises a task. A booking from a chat you handled is credited only when you choose &quot;I sourced this client&quot; on the quote or offer.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-when-the-visitor-leaves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When the visitor leaves</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A visitor not seen on the site for 10 minutes has left (Settings &gt; Program, &quot;Live chat: a visitor not seen on the site for this many minutes has left&quot;).</li><li>No phone or email: the chat closes by itself, marked <b class="gd-ui">Visitor left, no contact</b>. It leaves the count and its alerts clear.</li><li>A phone or email (typed in the chat, left in the contact box, or on their renter account): the chat stays open as <b class="gd-ui">Follow up by text/email</b>, out of the count, and customer service gets the task &quot;Follow up by text/email&quot; in their queue. Text or email them, then mark the task done.</li><li>A visitor who comes back to the site opens the chat again where it was.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-when-the-assistant-does-not-answer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When the assistant does not answer</h2><p class="gd-p">The assistant answers first, within seconds, and asks for a phone number or email early so we can follow up. It hands over when the visitor asks for a person or when it is not sure.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>When it cannot answer, Live chat shows <b class="gd-ui">AI replies paused</b> with the reason: turned off in Settings, today&#39;s live share of the free AI allowance used, or the last reply failed. The chat goes to a person and the conversation shows a staff note (only staff see it).</li><li>Common questions (the deposit, age and licence, how booking works, cancellation, hours, delivery) are answered from our own facts with no AI use.</li><li>The free AI allowance is shared by tier (open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Usage</b>): the staff assistant keeps 30%, live features (visitor chat, the phone line, the readers) have 50%, background writing 10%. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the shares</b> to change them.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-the-assistant-s-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The assistant&#39;s settings</h2><p class="gd-p">In Program settings, &quot;Live visitors and live chat&quot;: the chat on or off, the AI first or not (on by default), its model (Llama 3.1 8B), the neurons it may use a day (6,000, a few hundred replies; then chats wait for a person), when a visitor has left (10 minutes), the greeting on car pages after some seconds (off by default), how long chats and visits are kept, as the privacy policy says: chats 12 months, the pages of a visit 90 days, the visit&#39;s summary in History 13 months, and the daily totals, which name no one, 3 years.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="live-visitors-and-live-chat-what-a-visitor-typed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What a visitor typed</h2><p class="gd-p">A visitor who typed contact details into a form shows them on their line: &quot;Typed into the booking request, not sent: Maya Chen, maya@example.com&quot;, with <b class="gd-ui">Email not confirmed</b> until they open the link we emailed, and <b class="gd-ui">Renter page</b>.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'text-alerts-email-text-or-both', 'chapter', 'texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line', 'Every renter, owner, investor and staff member chooses how we reach them: Email, Text or Both. Texts go only to a phone they verified with a code, from the CarmaCars number, and each has a link to the page. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.

## Who gets what

- **Email**: emails only. **Text**: a short text instead of the email. **Both**: a text and the email.
- Not chosen yet: Both for someone with a verified phone and an email, Text for an account made by phone without an email, otherwise Email.
- No verified phone, a number that replied STOP, a US number while US texting waits for A2P 10DLC, or a number outside Canada and the US: email only.
- Signed agreements, statements, receipts, invoices and notices are always emailed when there is an email address. Someone on Text also gets a text with a link to view or download it in their portal.
- Every customer email has its own short text: renters, owners, investors, additional drivers, co-signers and leads. Only the sign-in and security emails (password reset, sign-in link, security notice, "Continue your request") are never texts. A review request or a come-back offer is texted only when its email may go (marketing consent).
- An additional driver''s or a co-signer''s link is texted to that person (their own account with a verified phone), never to the renter or owner.

## A person''s channel

Open the renter, owner or investor under People. The card **How we reach them** shows what they chose, what is used now and why, their verified phone, texts in the last 30 days and any STOP or START. Press **Change** to set it (recorded in the audit log). Customer service and Sales can change a renter''s or owner''s; an investor''s only Admins.

## STOP, START and quiet hours

- A reply STOP (or OPT OUT, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) stops texts to the number at once; texts waiting are not sent and their emails go instead. START turns texts back on. Every STOP and START is logged.
- Quo sends no confirmation, so we do: one text right away (quiet hours do not apply), "CarmaCars: you''re unsubscribed and won''t get more texts. Reply START to resubscribe." after STOP, and "CarmaCars: texts are back on. Reply STOP to opt out." after START. Once per change; the card How we reach them shows it as confirmed by text. A STOP or START you set by hand, or a carrier block, sends nothing.
- The first automated text to a number, and the first after START, ends "Reply STOP to opt out."
- Quiet hours, 9 pm to 8 am Toronto time: texts that are not urgent wait and go at 8 am. Urgent: late return notices, pickup and return details on the day, breakdown, accident and a disabled car.
- A text that is not sent after all (STOP, Quo refuses it, the person chose email meanwhile) sends the email it replaced.

## The settings and the texts

**Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**: on or off, the defaults, the quiet hours, the STOP line, US numbers, and the text of each notification with a preview (edit, switch off, mark urgent). A text names CarmaCars, keeps {{link}}, has no long dash and is at most 320 characters; 160 is one text. The two confirmation texts (after STOP and START) are in the same settings. The generic text built from the email''s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.

## Texts a day

Site health on **To do** has **Texts today**: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.

## Phone alerts

Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**; iOS 16.4 or later).

- What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts.
- Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.
- Your own: **Settings** > **My phone alerts**.
- On or off for everyone: **Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**, "Phone alerts".
- Setup: alerts need two keys in the vault, `deploy_vapid_public_key` and `deploy_vapid_private_key`. Until they are there the cards are hidden and **My phone alerts** says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.
', 'Text alerts: email, text or both', 'Each person''s channel, what is always emailed, STOP and START, quiet hours, US numbers, the texts and the daily count.',
  'Every renter, owner, investor and staff member chooses how we reach them: Email, Text or Both. Texts go only to a phone they verified with a code, from the CarmaCars number, and each has a link to the page. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.

## Who gets what

- **Email**: emails only. **Text**: a short text instead of the email. **Both**: a text and the email.
- Not chosen yet: Both for someone with a verified phone and an email, Text for an account made by phone without an email, otherwise Email.
- No verified phone, a number that replied STOP, a US number while US texting waits for A2P 10DLC, or a number outside Canada and the US: email only.
- Signed agreements, statements, receipts, invoices and notices are always emailed when there is an email address. Someone on Text also gets a text with a link to view or download it in their portal.
- Every customer email has its own short text: renters, owners, investors, additional drivers, co-signers and leads. Only the sign-in and security emails (password reset, sign-in link, security notice, "Continue your request") are never texts. A review request or a come-back offer is texted only when its email may go (marketing consent).
- An additional driver''s or a co-signer''s link is texted to that person (their own account with a verified phone), never to the renter or owner.

## A person''s channel

Open the renter, owner or investor under People. The card **How we reach them** shows what they chose, what is used now and why, their verified phone, texts in the last 30 days and any STOP or START. Press **Change** to set it (recorded in the audit log). Customer service and Sales can change a renter''s or owner''s; an investor''s only Admins.

## STOP, START and quiet hours

- A reply STOP (or OPT OUT, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) stops texts to the number at once; texts waiting are not sent and their emails go instead. START turns texts back on. Every STOP and START is logged.
- Quo sends no confirmation, so we do: one text right away (quiet hours do not apply), "CarmaCars: you''re unsubscribed and won''t get more texts. Reply START to resubscribe." after STOP, and "CarmaCars: texts are back on. Reply STOP to opt out." after START. Once per change; the card How we reach them shows it as confirmed by text. A STOP or START you set by hand, or a carrier block, sends nothing.
- The first automated text to a number, and the first after START, ends "Reply STOP to opt out."
- Quiet hours, 9 pm to 8 am Toronto time: texts that are not urgent wait and go at 8 am. Urgent: late return notices, pickup and return details on the day, breakdown, accident and a disabled car.
- A text that is not sent after all (STOP, Quo refuses it, the person chose email meanwhile) sends the email it replaced.

## The settings and the texts

**Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**: on or off, the defaults, the quiet hours, the STOP line, US numbers, and the text of each notification with a preview (edit, switch off, mark urgent). A text names CarmaCars, keeps {{link}}, has no long dash and is at most 320 characters; 160 is one text. The two confirmation texts (after STOP and START) are in the same settings. The generic text built from the email''s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.

## Booking start and end

Every booking gets these by itself, by email, text and phone alert (each person''s channel), once each, and again only when the time changes (an extension, a new pickup time):

| When | The renter gets |
| --- | --- |
| The day before pickup | What to bring, where and when |
| About 2 hours before pickup | "See you at 2:00 pm today", the place and what to bring |
| 30 minutes after a pickup nobody recorded | "You''re all set", the return time and place |
| The day before the return | The return time and place, fuel and keys |
| About 3 hours before the return | "Your rental ends at 5:00 pm", fuel, clean, all keys and a one-tap Extend link |
| At the return time | "Your booking ended at 5:00 pm", return now or extend |
| 15 minutes late | T13, the late notice |
| 2 hours late | T14, the final notice |

- A booking whose pickup nobody recorded counts as out: it gets the end messages, the late notices and the late tasks like a rental on rent. Its status stays as it is.
- The late notices and the short reminders go from 7 am to 10 pm. Overnight they wait until 7 am; a car returned in the night gets nothing.
- The late panel''s **Send T13** and **Send T14** send the same notices: never twice.
- An insurer-billed booking messages the renter too: they hold the car.
- **Pickup not recorded**: 30 minutes after the pickup time with nothing recorded, Fleet gets the task "Record pickup for CC-xxxxx, or mark no-show" and the field staff of the handover an alert and a text. At 3 hours the Admins get an alert and a task. They close by themselves once the pickup is recorded or the booking is cancelled.
- **Not back**: 15 minutes after the return time with no return recorded, the field staff of the return and the Admins get an alert and a text with the renter''s name and phone, at any hour.
- Each moment has its switch, all on: **Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**, "Booking start and end". The text of each is in the list of texts on the same page.

## Texts a day

Site health on **To do** has **Texts today**: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.

## Phone alerts

Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**; iOS 16.4 or later).

- What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts.
- Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.
- Your own: **Settings** > **My phone alerts**.
- On or off for everyone: **Settings** > **All settings**, **Text alerts**, "Phone alerts".
- Setup: nothing to do. The deploy makes the two keys alerts need once and keeps them; until the first deploy after this release the cards are hidden and **My phone alerts** says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.
