  '<p class="gd-p">Every renter, owner, investor and staff member chooses how we reach them: Email, Text or Both. Texts go only to a phone they verified with a code, from the CarmaCars number, and each has a link to the page. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.</p><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-who-gets-what" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who gets what</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Email</b>: emails only. <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a short text instead of the email. <b class="gd-ui">Both</b>: a text and the email.</li><li>Not chosen yet: Both for someone with a verified phone and an email, Text for an account made by phone without an email, otherwise Email.</li><li>No verified phone, a number that replied STOP, a US number while US texting waits for A2P 10DLC, or a number outside Canada and the US: email only.</li><li>Signed agreements, statements, receipts, invoices and notices are always emailed when there is an email address. Someone on Text also gets a text with a link to view or download it in their portal.</li><li>Every customer email has its own short text: renters, owners, investors, additional drivers, co-signers and leads. Only the sign-in and security emails (password reset, sign-in link, security notice, &quot;Continue your request&quot;) are never texts. A review request or a come-back offer is texted only when its email may go (marketing consent).</li><li>An additional driver&#39;s or a co-signer&#39;s link is texted to that person (their own account with a verified phone), never to the renter or owner.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-a-person-s-channel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A person&#39;s channel</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the renter, owner or investor under People. The card <b class="gd-ui">How we reach them</b> shows what they chose, what is used now and why, their verified phone, texts in the last 30 days and any STOP or START. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to set it (recorded in the audit log). Customer service and Sales can change a renter&#39;s or owner&#39;s; an investor&#39;s only Admins.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-stop-start-and-quiet-hours" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">STOP, START and quiet hours</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A reply STOP (or OPT OUT, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) stops texts to the number at once; texts waiting are not sent and their emails go instead. START turns texts back on. Every STOP and START is logged.</li><li>Quo sends no confirmation, so we do: one text right away (quiet hours do not apply), &quot;CarmaCars: you&#39;re unsubscribed and won&#39;t get more texts. Reply START to resubscribe.&quot; after STOP, and &quot;CarmaCars: texts are back on. Reply STOP to opt out.&quot; after START. Once per change; the card How we reach them shows it as confirmed by text. A STOP or START you set by hand, or a carrier block, sends nothing.</li><li>The first automated text to a number, and the first after START, ends &quot;Reply STOP to opt out.&quot;</li><li>Quiet hours, 9 pm to 8 am Toronto time: texts that are not urgent wait and go at 8 am. Urgent: late return notices, pickup and return details on the day, breakdown, accident and a disabled car.</li><li>A text that is not sent after all (STOP, Quo refuses it, the person chose email meanwhile) sends the email it replaced.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-the-settings-and-the-texts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The settings and the texts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>: on or off, the defaults, the quiet hours, the STOP line, US numbers, and the text of each notification with a preview (edit, switch off, mark urgent). A text names CarmaCars, keeps {{link}}, has no long dash and is at most 320 characters; 160 is one text. The two confirmation texts (after STOP and START) are in the same settings. The generic text built from the email&#39;s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-booking-start-and-end" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booking start and end</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking gets these by itself, by email, text and phone alert (each person&#39;s channel), once each, and again only when the time changes (an extension, a new pickup time):</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">The renter gets</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The day before pickup</td><td>What to bring, where and when</td></tr><tr><td>About 2 hours before pickup</td><td>&quot;See you at 2:00 pm today&quot;, the place and what to bring</td></tr><tr><td>30 minutes after a pickup nobody recorded</td><td>&quot;You&#39;re all set&quot;, the return time and place</td></tr><tr><td>The day before the return</td><td>The return time and place, fuel and keys</td></tr><tr><td>About 3 hours before the return</td><td>&quot;Your rental ends at 5:00 pm&quot;, fuel, clean, all keys and a one-tap Extend link</td></tr><tr><td>At the return time</td><td>&quot;Your booking ended at 5:00 pm&quot;, return now or extend</td></tr><tr><td>15 minutes late</td><td>T13, the late notice</td></tr><tr><td>2 hours late</td><td>T14, the final notice</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A booking whose pickup nobody recorded counts as out: it gets the end messages, the late notices and the late tasks like a rental on rent. Its status stays as it is.</li><li>The late notices and the short reminders go from 7 am to 10 pm. Overnight they wait until 7 am; a car returned in the night gets nothing.</li><li>The late panel&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send T14</b> send the same notices: never twice.</li><li>An insurer-billed booking messages the renter too: they hold the car.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded</b>: 30 minutes after the pickup time with nothing recorded, Fleet gets the task &quot;Record pickup for CC-xxxxx, or mark no-show&quot; and the field staff of the handover an alert and a text. At 3 hours the Admins get an alert and a task. They close by themselves once the pickup is recorded or the booking is cancelled.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Not back</b>: 15 minutes after the return time with no return recorded, the field staff of the return and the Admins get an alert and a text with the renter&#39;s name and phone, at any hour.</li><li>Each moment has its switch, all on: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Booking start and end&quot;. The text of each is in the list of texts on the same page.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-texts-a-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts a day</h2><p class="gd-p">Site health on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> has <b class="gd-ui">Texts today</b>: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>; iOS 16.4 or later).</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts.</li><li>Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.</li><li>Your own: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My phone alerts</b>.</li><li>On or off for everyone: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Phone alerts&quot;.</li><li>Setup: nothing to do. The deploy makes the two keys alerts need once and keeps them; until the first deploy after this release the cards are hidden and <b class="gd-ui">My phone alerts</b> says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'discount-games-and-leads', 'chapter', 'text-alerts-email-text-or-both', 'Visitors who are not signed in get one quick game: spin the wheel, scratch to reveal, quick blackjack, cup shuffle, Plinko, the card pack, coin flip, dice roll, slot machine, prize drop or mystery box. Every play wins a promo code or another go. To see the code they give a first name and an email (a mobile number is optional), so you get a lead. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.

## What the visitor sees

- On the 2nd page view (any page) or after 30 seconds on the site, whichever first, or (on a computer) when the mouse heads for the tabs. A card slides in at the bottom; on a phone it is a sheet at the bottom, never a full-screen block, and it always closes.
- Never for someone signed in, never on booking, pay, sign or sign-in pages, never on the first page of a visit from a search engine on a phone, never over the cookie banner; no new game for someone already known by email or with a booking request in progress. Once a visit by default, and again on every new visit (a visit ends after 30 minutes away), also when they closed it without playing. Settings > Discount games has Preview the game, to see it any time, signed in or not.
- After claiming a code: no game for the rest of that visit. A day after their latest claim the game comes back on their next visit with the usual timings, a new game and a new draw, and they can win another code. The day counts for the browser, the email, the mobile number and (in the request-to-book form) the account; within it the game says when they can play again. A visitor known only through their own claim still gets it; one known through a booking request, the chat, a sign-in or as a renter does not.
- Won and not claimed: a small badge "Your 5% off is saved" with **Get my code** and **Play again** stays on the pages. On a later visit, at the moment a first game would show, the prize pops up by itself once as a small slide-in at the bottom ("Your 5% off is still waiting", the same two buttons), never as a card over the page; closed, it does not come back in that visit. Until they claim it or the prize ends after 14 days.
- **Play again** on a prize not claimed: a new, different game with a new draw. They keep the better of the two prizes and the other is closed, so there is only ever one code to claim: the card says "You won 15% off" or "You keep your 5% off". Once a visit and once a day (a setting).
- Every play wins: 5% off (54 in 100), 10% off (25), another go (15), 15% off (4), $50 off a rental of 3 days or more (1), 25% off up to $150 (0.6), $100 off a rental of 4 days or more (0.3) or one free day on a rental of 3 days or more (0.1). The prize is decided before the game starts; the game only shows it. The short terms with the game list the prizes and say the chances differ.
- Another go: the card says "You won another go!" and **Play again** starts a second, different game whose prize is drawn from the discounts only, so it always ends in a code. One replay at a time; it is never a code itself. Closed before pressing it, the card offers it again next time.
- The code (for example WIN-7KQ4-XM2P) comes off the rental charge only, up to $75 for a percentage, on one booking, within 7 days, one code a day per person, email, phone and device, never with another code. An earlier code not used yet stays good until it ends. The email with the code goes either way; a reminder goes 3 days before its last day and another the day before (Promo codes). Offers only with the marketing box ticked.
- On this device the code fills itself into the promo code box of the request form. Like every promo code, the discount is shared with the owner in the split.

## Leads

**Bookings** > **Renter leads**.

1. The tiles: plays, claims, codes on booking requests, bookings, revenue and discounts from game codes in the last 30 days, then the same by game and by prize (Play again shows its plays; it has no claims).
2. Each claim: when, the name (and "on the site now"), email and phone, the prize and game, the code and whether it is used (with the booking), marketing consent, and the visit: cars and pages viewed, minutes, city and device. A person who won again shows "2nd code of 2" under the name on each of their lines.
3. Press **Call** or **Email**, then **Contacted** (it is yours). **Close** with a reason when there is nothing more to do. A booking with the code marks the lead converted by itself.
4. A visitor who viewed 3 cars or more also gets a Sales task, for example "Claimed 10% off, viewed 6 cars: Maya". It closes when the code goes on a request. A new code while that task is open is added to it, not a second task.

## Contact details typed into forms

**Bookings** > **Renter leads**, the card "Typed into forms" at the top.

1. When someone types a name, email or phone into the request to book, the contact form, List your car, the owner application, Create an account, the discount game or the chat, it is saved as soon as each field is valid, even if they never press Send.
2. Each line: when, the name (and "On the site now"), email and phone, the form, and Sent or Not sent. "Email not confirmed" means the account was opened from the form and the person has not opened the link we emailed them yet.
3. After 30 minutes without sending, To do shows "Unfinished request from Maya Chen: follow up" (not raised from 23:00 to 07:00, the quiet hours of the site alerts). Call or email them; the task closes by itself when they send the form.
4. Only what they typed is saved, and never used for offers without their consent.

> Good to know: A new email gets an account at once (no password, email not confirmed) and one email "Continue your request" 30 minutes later, between 9:00 and 21:00. Until they open its link they cannot accept an offer, sign, pay or upload documents. An account never confirmed closes after 30 days; the lead stays. It is on by default; the times and the To do are in **Settings** > **Program**, the card "Forms left unfinished".

## Settings

**Settings** > **Discount games**.

- On or off, the cap for percentage codes ($75), how long a code is good for (7 days), when it shows (2nd page view, 30 seconds, exit intent), the days a visitor keeps their prize (14: closing never draws a new one, and a prize not claimed pops up again until then), the days after a claim before the game comes back (1; 0 is one code per person ever), how often Play again works on a prize not claimed (once a day; 0 turns it off), and the cars viewed for a Sales task (3). The reminders before a code ends are under Promo codes.
- At most one game a visit by default (a setting), and a visit ends after 30 minutes away (a setting): the next page brings the game again. With more than one a visit, the next card shows on their 3rd page view after a close (any page) or 2 minutes later, whichever first; no daily cap unless you set one. A prize waiting for them pops up once a visit only. All are settings. Never on booking, payment or signing pages; the request-to-book form has its own game.
- Prizes and games: each prize with its percent, dollars or free days, a minimum rental length, its cap and its chance, or Play again (another go, at most one); each game''s weight (0 turns it off). Press **Save prizes and games**. Codes already sent keep their value.
