**Settings** > **Reviews**: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.

1. When review requests go: the check-in (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-in), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.
2. The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile''s own review link.
3. Google Business Profile: press **Connect Google** and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.
4. A clear match stops that renter''s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press **Confirm**, **Not this renter** or **Match to a booking**.

> Tip: Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and "I already left a review", Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.

### Pair the card reader
**Settings** > **Card reader**. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open **Settings**, then **Generate pairing code**. Type the three words in **Pairing code**, name the reader (Front desk) and press **Pair reader**. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. **Remove** takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account''s statement descriptor.

### Rewards
**Settings** > **Rewards**. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter''s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.

1. **Ways to earn**: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend''s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows "Received reward points"), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter''s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).
2. **Tiers**: Member, Silver from 10 rental days in 12 months (5% off) and Gold from 30 (10% off), with a perk staff honour on request. The discount is a promo code of the renter''s own.
3. Points, tier discounts and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code.
4. **Google reviews claimed** lists every claim; **Reverse** takes the points back with a reason. **A renter''s points**: find the renter, then **Add or take off points** with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).

### Setup checklist
**Settings** shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars'' own accounts. **Add to Apple Wallet** stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker''s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.</p><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-settings-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Settings page</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with <b class="gd-ui">Open site settings</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Program settings: every timing and policy value.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Forms: Blind Spot&#39;s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:33%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:84.9%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company&#39;s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes and Quick replies.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">My profile</b>: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole (&quot;Good morning, Abbas and Mahad&quot; on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the greeting name</b>, type it and save.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-program-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Program settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turnaround between trips: the time held between two trips. The cleaning block after a trip is this time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month&#39;s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the defaults</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-out besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Change a value and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:22%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:27.8%;top:49%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-lead-time-pricing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lead-time pricing</h2><p class="gd-p">A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: Lead-time pricing is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); <b class="gd-ui">Add a tier</b> adds one, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer</b> is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save lead-time pricing</b>. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What it touches</th><th scope="col">How</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The rental charge</td><td>The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, &quot;Short-notice pricing +10%&quot; or &quot;Booked ahead −5%&quot;. Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons</td></tr><tr><td>When it is worked out</td><td>When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. &quot;From $X a day&quot; stays at the base rate</td></tr><tr><td>When it is locked</td><td>On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage</td></tr><tr><td>Other discounts</td><td>The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it</td></tr><tr><td>Owner revenue and commissions</td><td>Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts</td></tr><tr><td>Staff</td><td>Change it on a booking under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b> on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; the car &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> &gt; Lead-time pricing for this car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-vehicle-class-rules" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle class rules</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle class rules</b>. How a new car&#39;s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a rule</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try a car</b> gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-official-serviceontario-forms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Official ServiceOntario forms</h2><p class="gd-p">The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. Each form shows &quot;Mapping to check&quot; (a draft is ready) or &quot;Official PDF in use&quot;. Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download a filled preview</b> for one car and check each value against the form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or &quot;Signed here by hand, in ink&quot;), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Press Save the mapping.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for owners</b>. Every owner&#39;s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with <b class="gd-ui">Record paper signature</b>. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A new version from ServiceOntario? Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload the official fillable PDF</b>: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company&#39;s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner&#39;s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form&#39;s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-blind-spot-rental-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Blind Spot rental agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental&#39;s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars&#39; rental agreement and Blind Spot&#39;s own. Blind Spot&#39;s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload Blind Spot&#39;s PDF</b> and choose Blind Spot&#39;s blank form (2 pages, A4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the filled sample</b>: a made-up booking on the form. <b class="gd-ui">Sample billed to an insurer</b> also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars&#39; HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative&#39;s signature instead of Sam&#39;s.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A new version of Blind Spot&#39;s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>, and bookings keep the version in use until then.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-out and check-in stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-out report (fuel out) and the check-in report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking&#39;s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter&#39;s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the &quot;Your signed rental agreement&quot; email. Admin &gt; Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-agreements-to-sign-investors-and-staff" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements to sign: investors and staff</h2><p class="gd-p">Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person&#39;s record and signed in their own portal, or on paper.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Investor: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b>. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Once the investor signs, the agreement shows <b class="gd-ui">Awaiting countersignature</b> on the investor&#39;s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press <b class="gd-ui">Countersign</b>. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Staff: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff</b>. Under Staff agreements, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b> beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field staff member&#39;s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Your own PDF instead? <b class="gd-ui">Send a PDF to sign</b> still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Signed on paper instead? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record paper signature</b> in the same place and upload the scan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Sent by mistake? Press <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> and give the reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-user-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The user guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Guides</b>. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press <b class="gd-ui">Show the preview</b> to see it as people will. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the draft</b>; each save is kept in the section&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a chapter</b>. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish version</b> (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-guides-keep-up-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The guides keep up by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal&#39;s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Such a section says <b class="gd-ui">Changed automatically on</b> and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide&#39;s editor. Not right? Open the section and press <b class="gd-ui">Revert</b>: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section&#39;s history. There is nothing to review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The card &quot;The guides keep up by themselves&quot; at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-insurers-and-the-other-lists" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Insurers and the other lists</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurer rates</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-promo-codes-end-dates-and-reminders" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Promo codes: end dates and reminders</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Promo codes</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.</li><li>A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.</li><li>A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with &quot;This code has expired&quot;.</li><li>A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.</li><li>The list shows each code&#39;s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-card-coverage-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> is the list renters see at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer&#39;s own document, and when it was last checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer&#39;s own document unticked and the summary&#39;s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-reviews-review-requests-and-google" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reviews: review requests and Google</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When review requests go: the check-in (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-in), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile&#39;s own review link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google Business Profile: press <b class="gd-ui">Connect Google</b> and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A clear match stops that renter&#39;s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and &quot;I already left a review&quot;, Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Pair the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card reader</b>. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Generate pairing code</b>. Type the three words in <b class="gd-ui">Pairing code</b>, name the reader (Front desk) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pair reader</b>. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account&#39;s statement descriptor.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Rewards</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b>. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter&#39;s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ways to earn</b>: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend&#39;s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows &quot;Received reward points&quot;), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter&#39;s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tiers</b>: Member, Silver from 10 rental days in 12 months (5% off) and Gold from 30 (10% off), with a perk staff honour on request. The discount is a promo code of the renter&#39;s own.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Points, tier discounts and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Google reviews claimed</b> lists every claim; <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> takes the points back with a reason. <b class="gd-ui">A renter&#39;s points</b>: find the renter, then <b class="gd-ui">Add or take off points</b> with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Setup checklist</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars&#39; own accounts. <b class="gd-ui">Add to Apple Wallet</b> stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker&#39;s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'usage-and-paid-usage', 'chapter', 'assistant', 'The plans CarmaCars runs on include a free allowance: AI, the website, image transformations, emails, the database and storage. When an allowance runs out, AI and photo features pause with a short message until it resets. Workers AI never runs into paid usage; for photos you are asked before anything is paid.

## The alerts

At 80% of an allowance you get one quiet card on **To do** and one email to the alert address. When it is used up, a second card and email.

1. Workers AI used up shows "Stopped for today, never paid": it starts again at midnight, Toronto time. There is nothing to allow.
2. A used-up image allowance shows "Included ... used up for this month: Allow paid usage". Press **Allow paid usage** to see what continuing costs at the current rates.
3. Choose until the end of today or this month, type the most it may cost (for example $1), and press the Allow button. Or press Keep paused.
4. Nobody answering keeps it paused: nothing is charged. Live chat goes to a person, AI copy waits with the template text, Turo emails are read by the rules, photos keep their original background, the assistant rests.
5. The website and the portals are never paused (that would stop bookings): their card shows the estimated cost, usually cents.

## Settings > Usage

Open **Settings**, then **Usage**: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.

1. Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app''s own record shows as Unmetered.
2. The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.
3. Press **Change the shares** to change the assistant''s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.
4. Press **Change the allowance** after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).
5. Database size and file storage are our own server''s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.
6. Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.

## Alerts by text and the banner

7. When a figure reaches 80% of its allowance, and again at 100% (the website''s CPU time also at 70%), every Admin with a verified phone gets a text, once per figure and level a month, outside the quiet hours. Turn it off in Program settings (Usage alerts: also text every Admin).
8. While a figure is at its warning level or past it, a banner at the top of **Today** says so: red past the allowance, amber before.

## Emails through Cloudflare first

9. The site''s emails go through Cloudflare Email Service first (3,000 a month included with Workers Paid), then Resend. Sign-in emails stay on Resend. Emails wait until midnight only when both are used. "Emails this month (Cloudflare)" counts them. It needs the one-time setup in docs/changes/2026-11-03-cloudflare-email.md.
10. "Texts this month (Quo)" counts the texts sent through the Quo API, about US$0.01 each, with the cost so far. The texts and the banner warn at 80% and 100% of the 300 a month set as the budget (**Change the allowance**).
', 'Usage and paid usage', 'Included allowances, the 80% and used-up alerts, Workers AI by feature (never paid), allowing paid usage for photos, what pauses and what never does.',
  'The plans CarmaCars runs on include a free allowance: AI, the website, image transformations, emails, the database and storage. When an allowance runs out, AI and photo features pause with a short message until it resets. Workers AI never runs into paid usage; for photos you are asked before anything is paid.

## The alerts

At 80% of an allowance you get one quiet card on **To do**. When it is used up, a second card. Usage alerts are never emailed (they used to count against the emails they warned about); the banner, the cards and the Usage page show them.

1. Workers AI used up shows "Stopped for today, never paid": it starts again at midnight, Toronto time. There is nothing to allow.
2. A used-up image allowance shows "Included ... used up for this month: Allow paid usage". Press **Allow paid usage** to see what continuing costs at the current rates.
3. Choose until the end of today or this month, type the most it may cost (for example $1), and press the Allow button. Or press Keep paused.
4. Nobody answering keeps it paused: nothing is charged. Live chat goes to a person, AI copy waits with the template text, Turo emails are read by the rules, photos keep their original background, the assistant rests.
5. The website and the portals are never paused (that would stop bookings): their card shows the estimated cost, usually cents.

## Settings > Usage

Open **Settings**, then **Usage**: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.

1. Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app''s own record shows as Unmetered.
2. The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.
3. Press **Change the shares** to change the assistant''s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.
4. Press **Change the allowance** after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).
5. Database size and file storage are our own server''s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.
6. Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.

## Alerts by text and the banner

7. When a figure reaches 80% of its allowance, and again at 100% (the website''s CPU time also at 70%), every Admin with a verified phone gets a text, once per figure and level a month, outside the quiet hours. Turn it off in Program settings (Usage alerts: also text every Admin).
8. The banner at the top of **Today** speaks in money. The website, requests, storage and texts are billed by use and never paused: their banner is red only when this month''s projected cost above the allowance reaches US$5 (Program settings, Usage: red banner and alert only from), and then you also get the text. Under it, one quiet grey line with the cost (usually cents) and no text. Workers AI, photos and Claude (they stop or pause) and the emails (held at 100 a day) keep their banner: red when used up, amber before.

## Emails through Cloudflare first

9. The site''s emails go through Cloudflare Email Service first (3,000 a month included with Workers Paid), then Resend. Sign-in emails stay on Resend. Emails wait until midnight only when both are used. "Emails this month (Cloudflare)" counts them. It needs a one-time setup: the **Emails** card at the top of the Usage page (open **Settings**, then **Usage**) says whether Cloudflare sends and, when it does not, lists the four steps; the emails banner links to them, and every deploy lists the step until it is done.
10. "Texts this month (Quo)" counts the texts sent through the Quo API, about US$0.01 each, with the cost so far. The texts and the banner warn at 80% and 100% of the 300 a month set as the budget (**Change the allowance**).
11. Crawlers: every search and AI crawler may read every page; a crawler that read a page in the last 3 days gets the saved copy, not a new render. If this month''s projected CPU cost above the allowance passes US$40 (Program settings, Crawlers), the AI training crawlers keep to the core pages until the month ends and a note on **To do** says so. Google, Bing and the AI search crawlers are never limited.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The plans CarmaCars runs on include a free allowance: AI, the website, image transformations, emails, the database and storage. When an allowance runs out, AI and photo features pause with a short message until it resets. Workers AI never runs into paid usage; for photos you are asked before anything is paid.</p><section class="gd-task" id="usage-and-paid-usage-the-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">At 80% of an allowance you get one quiet card on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>. When it is used up, a second card. Usage alerts are never emailed (they used to count against the emails they warned about); the banner, the cards and the Usage page show them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Workers AI used up shows &quot;Stopped for today, never paid&quot;: it starts again at midnight, Toronto time. There is nothing to allow.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A used-up image allowance shows &quot;Included ... used up for this month: Allow paid usage&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Allow paid usage</b> to see what continuing costs at the current rates.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose until the end of today or this month, type the most it may cost (for example $1), and press the Allow button. Or press Keep paused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody answering keeps it paused: nothing is charged. Live chat goes to a person, AI copy waits with the template text, Turo emails are read by the rules, photos keep their original background, the assistant rests.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The website and the portals are never paused (that would stop bookings): their card shows the estimated cost, usually cents.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="usage-and-paid-usage-settings-usage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settings &gt; Usage</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Usage</b>: every service, used against included, when it resets, paid usage and the last 30 days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Workers AI by feature, at the top: the neurons each feature used today and in the last 7 days (the staff assistant, visitor chat, the phone line, search copy, listing copy, guide upkeep, Turo emails, the readers), and what each share has left now. Use Cloudflare counted beyond the app&#39;s own record shows as Unmetered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The day is shared in three: 70% is kept for the staff assistant; visitor chat, the phone line and the readers share the rest; background writing (search copy, listing copy, guide rewrites, Turo emails) gets 10%, and from 9 pm what is left of the day, less a small cushion for the assistant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the shares</b> to change the assistant&#39;s reserve, the background share, the release hour or the cushion.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the allowance</b> after a plan change (for example a Resend upgrade, or a larger disk on our server).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Database size and file storage are our own server&#39;s: near the allowance, clean up or move to a larger server disk. Nothing is billed by use.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Emails cannot be paid on the free plan: when the daily or monthly count is used, booking, payment and sign-in emails still go first and the others wait. A banner on To do says so.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="usage-and-paid-usage-alerts-by-text-and-the-banner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alerts by text and the banner</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="7"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">When a figure reaches 80% of its allowance, and again at 100% (the website&#39;s CPU time also at 70%), every Admin with a verified phone gets a text, once per figure and level a month, outside the quiet hours. Turn it off in Program settings (Usage alerts: also text every Admin).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">The banner at the top of <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> speaks in money. The website, requests, storage and texts are billed by use and never paused: their banner is red only when this month&#39;s projected cost above the allowance reaches US$5 (Program settings, Usage: red banner and alert only from), and then you also get the text. Under it, one quiet grey line with the cost (usually cents) and no text. Workers AI, photos and Claude (they stop or pause) and the emails (held at 100 a day) keep their banner: red when used up, amber before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="usage-and-paid-usage-emails-through-cloudflare-first" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Emails through Cloudflare first</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="9"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">The site&#39;s emails go through Cloudflare Email Service first (3,000 a month included with Workers Paid), then Resend. Sign-in emails stay on Resend. Emails wait until midnight only when both are used. &quot;Emails this month (Cloudflare)&quot; counts them. It needs a one-time setup: the <b class="gd-ui">Emails</b> card at the top of the Usage page (open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Usage</b>) says whether Cloudflare sends and, when it does not, lists the four steps; the emails banner links to them, and every deploy lists the step until it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Texts this month (Quo)&quot; counts the texts sent through the Quo API, about US$0.01 each, with the cost so far. The texts and the banner warn at 80% and 100% of the 300 a month set as the budget (<b class="gd-ui">Change the allowance</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Crawlers: every search and AI crawler may read every page; a crawler that read a page in the last 3 days gets the saved copy, not a new render. If this month&#39;s projected CPU cost above the allowance passes US$40 (Program settings, Crawlers), the AI training crawlers keep to the core pages until the month ends and a note on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> says so. Google, Bing and the AI search crawlers are never limited.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'email-backups-and-site-health', 'chapter', 'maintenance-and-service', 'Keep an eye on email use against the daily limit, the nightly backup and the occasional error page.

## Email

**Settings** > **Email log**

1. The banner shows today''s emails against the daily limit. From 80, Admins get a notice; near the limit, digests and marketing wait first and booking and sign-in emails are held last.
2. Filter the Outbox: All, Queued, Held, Sent, Failed, Suppressed or Skipped.
3. Open an email to **Resend** or **Cancel** it.
4. Suppressions: **Suppress an address** stops all mail to it; **Lift** undoes it.
5. **Text it instead** on a held or queued email sends it at once by text to the person''s mobile, with the link to their page. The email still goes when the limit lifts.

> Tip: When the limit is reached, booking and pickup emails (the confirmation, the agreement and signing links, pickup details, the handover, payment links and signing codes) go by text on their own, once each. Sign-in then opens on the phone option, and signing codes are offered by text first. Turn it off in **Settings** > **All settings** > Site settings, Email limit.

![](/guides/img/admin-23-email-desktop-dad31712.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/messages; pins: 1 56.5 31.7, 2 35.5 41.8, 3 81.9 52.6, 4 26.6 22.9")

## Backups

- The database is backed up every night, encrypted, kept for 30 days and test-restored on the spot.
- Every Monday the newest backup is checked again: it must be under 30 hours old and restore cleanly.
- A failed backup, or none for 30 hours, opens a site alert: an email (outside the quiet hours), a task and a line on To do. Tell your developer the same day.
- Keep a copy of the backup key in the company password manager. Without it no backup can be read.

## Site health and alerts

**Today** > **To do**, the Site health card at the bottom.

1. Every 5 minutes the site checks itself: the home page, a car page, the sign-in page and the site''s health check, and also emails, scheduled jobs, the nightly backup and Stripe payments.
2. Each line shows Working, Problem, Waiting for the website deploy or Not checked yet, what was found and how many checks failed in the last 24 hours.
3. Short problems, such as a single Error 1102, only show here and in your morning digest ("Site check: 6 failed checks in the last 24 hours, no alert email").
4. An email goes to rent@carmacars.ca only for a real outage: a page failing every check for 15 minutes, emails failing for 30 minutes, the nightly backup failing, or Stripe failing for 30 minutes. It also raises an urgent task and "Site problems found by the site check" first on To do. A failed scheduled job is never emailed.
5. At most 3 alert emails a day, and none from 11 pm to 7 am unless the whole site has been down for an hour. An outage held overnight is emailed at 7 am if it lasts. One "Recovered" email follows each alert, and the task closes by itself.
6. "Waiting for the website deploy" on the health check means the database was updated before the website: nothing is wrong, and it turns to Working after the deploy.

> Good to know: The alert address, the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours are in Program settings, "Site check".

## When a page shows "Error 1102"

Our web host''s free plan sometimes stops a page that takes too long. Reload the page; you are still signed in. Moving to the Workers Paid plan removes it.
